      "updated": 1763924447569,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Short Polling (HTTP Polling / Regular Polling):\n   - Client sends a request to the server at fixed intervals (e.g., every 1 second).\n   - Server responds immediately, even if there is NO new data.\n   - Client keeps repeating this.\n   - Simple but very inefficient.\n   - Wastes bandwidth and increases server load because most responses are empty.\n   - Causes noticeable delay (because client waits until next interval).\n\n2. Long Polling:\n   - Client sends a request but the server does NOT respond immediately.\n   - Server holds the request open until new data is available.\n   - When new data arrives → server responds → connection closes → client instantly sends a new request.\n   - Feels almost \"real-time\" while still using normal HTTP.\n   - More efficient than regular polling because there are fewer useless responses.\n   - Still not as efficient as WebSockets because every message requires a full HTTP request/response cycle.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Short Polling (HTTP Polling / Regular Polling):\n   - Client sends a request to the server at fixed intervals (e.g., every 1 second).\n   - Server responds immediately, even if there is NO new data.\n   - Client keeps repeating this.\n   - Simple but very inefficient.\n   - Wastes bandwidth and increases server load because most responses are empty.\n   - Causes noticeable delay (because client waits until next interval).\n\n2. Long Polling:\n   - Client sends a request but the server does NOT respond immediately.\n   - Server holds the request open until new data is available.\n   - When new data arrives → server responds → connection closes → client instantly sends a new request.\n   - Feels almost \"real-time\" while still using normal HTTP.\n   - More efficient than regular polling because there are fewer useless responses.\n   - Still not as efficient as WebSockets because every message requires a full HTTP request/response cycle.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
