      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here’s a **simple code comparison** for **WebSockets vs Socket.IO**, showing how real-time communication differs:\n\n```\n1️⃣ WebSocket (Raw):\n\n// Server (Node.js)\nconst WebSocket = require('ws');\nconst wss = new WebSocket.Server({ port: 4444 });\n\nwss.on('connection', (ws) => {\n  console.log('Client connected');\n\n  ws.on('message', (message) => {\n    console.log('Received:', message);\n    ws.send(`Server says: ${message}`);\n  });\n\n  ws.on('close', () => {\n    console.log('Client disconnected');\n  });\n});\n\n// Client (Browser)\nconst ws = new WebSocket('ws://localhost:4444');\n\nws.onopen = () => ws.send('Hello server!');\nws.onmessage = (e) => console.log('Server:', e.data);\n```\n\n```\n2️⃣ Socket.IO (Library on top of WebSocket):\n\n// Server (Node.js + Express)\nconst express = require('express');\nconst app = express();\nconst http = require('http').createServer(app);\nconst io = require('socket.io')(http);\n\nio.on('connection', (socket) => {\n  console.log('Client connected');\n\n  socket.on('chatMessage', (msg) => {\n    console.log('Message:', msg);\n    socket.emit('chatMessage', `Server: ${msg}`);\n  });\n\n  socket.on('disconnect', () => {\n    console.log('Client disconnected');\n  });\n});\n\nhttp.listen(4444, () => console.log('Server running on 4444'));\n\n// Client (Browser)\nconst socket = io('http://localhost:4444');\n\nsocket.emit('chatMessage', 'Hello server!');\nsocket.on('chatMessage', (msg) => console.log(msg));\n```\n\n**Key Differences in Code:**\n\n* **WebSocket**:\n  *Raw API*, sends/receives plain messages, you handle reconnects, events, and fallback manually.\n* **Socket.IO**:\n  *Event-based API*, automatically handles reconnections, fallbacks (long polling, XHR, JSONP), and room/broadcast support.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here’s a **simple code comparison** for **WebSockets vs Socket.IO**, showing how real-time communication differs:\n\n```\n1️⃣ WebSocket (Raw):\n\n// Server (Node.js)\nconst WebSocket = require('ws');\nconst wss = new WebSocket.Server({ port: 4444 });\n\nwss.on('connection', (ws) => {\n  console.log('Client connected');\n\n  ws.on('message', (message) => {\n    console.log('Received:', message);\n    ws.send(`Server says: ${message}`);\n  });\n\n  ws.on('close', () => {\n    console.log('Client disconnected');\n  });\n});\n\n// Client (Browser)\nconst ws = new WebSocket('ws://localhost:4444');\n\nws.onopen = () => ws.send('Hello server!');\nws.onmessage = (e) => console.log('Server:', e.data);\n```\n\n```\n2️⃣ Socket.IO (Library on top of WebSocket):\n\n// Server (Node.js + Express)\nconst express = require('express');\nconst app = express();\nconst http = require('http').createServer(app);\nconst io = require('socket.io')(http);\n\nio.on('connection', (socket) => {\n  console.log('Client connected');\n\n  socket.on('chatMessage', (msg) => {\n    console.log('Message:', msg);\n    socket.emit('chatMessage', `Server: ${msg}`);\n  });\n\n  socket.on('disconnect', () => {\n    console.log('Client disconnected');\n  });\n});\n\nhttp.listen(4444, () => console.log('Server running on 4444'));\n\n// Client (Browser)\nconst socket = io('http://localhost:4444');\n\nsocket.emit('chatMessage', 'Hello server!');\nsocket.on('chatMessage', (msg) => console.log(msg));\n```\n\n**Key Differences in Code:**\n\n* **WebSocket**:\n  *Raw API*, sends/receives plain messages, you handle reconnects, events, and fallback manually.\n* **Socket.IO**:\n  *Event-based API*, automatically handles reconnections, fallbacks (long polling, XHR, JSONP), and room/broadcast support.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
