      "updated": 1763927629212,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Here’s a **code-focused comparison of WebSocket vs Socket.IO**, showing exactly what you’d write for similar functionality like broadcasting or rooms:\n\n```\n1️⃣ WebSocket (raw)\n\nconst WebSocket = require('ws');\nconst wss = new WebSocket.Server({ port: 4444 });\n\nwss.on('connection', (ws) => {\n  console.log('Client connected');\n\n  // Sending message to this client\n  ws.send('Welcome!');\n\n  // Manual broadcast to all other clients\n  ws.on('message', (message) => {\n    wss.clients.forEach(client => {\n      if (client !== ws && client.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n        client.send(`Broadcast: ${message}`);\n      }\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```\n2️⃣ Socket.IO (with rooms & broadcast)\n\nconst express = require('express');\nconst app = express();\nconst http = require('http').createServer(app);\nconst io = require('socket.io')(http);\n\nio.on('connection', (socket) => {\n  console.log('Client connected');\n\n  // Join a room\n  socket.join('room1');\n\n  // Send to this client\n  socket.emit('message', 'Welcome!');\n\n  // Broadcast to everyone else in room1\n  socket.on('chatMessage', (msg) => {\n    socket.to('room1').emit('message', `Broadcast: ${msg}`);\n  });\n\n  // Broadcast to all except sender (default room)\n  socket.on('globalMessage', (msg) => {\n    socket.broadcast.emit('message', `Global: ${msg}`);\n  });\n});\n\nhttp.listen(4444, () => console.log('Server running on 4444'));\n```\n\n**Key Points in Code Comparison:**\n\n| Feature                   | WebSocket                      | Socket.IO                                 |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Broadcast to all clients  | Manual loop over `wss.clients` | `io.emit()` or `socket.broadcast.emit()`  |\n| Rooms / channels          | Not built-in                   | `socket.join('room')`, `io.to('room')`    |\n| Event-based communication | Only `message` events          | Named events: `socket.on('event')`        |\n| Auto-reconnect            | No                             | Yes, built-in                             |\n| Fallbacks (long polling)  | No                             | Yes, automatically handles older browsers |\n\nThis shows **exactly what extra code you’d have to write in raw WebSocket** vs **Socket.IO where it’s built-in**.\n",
      "fontSize": 21.795884526503066,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Here’s a **code-focused comparison of WebSocket vs Socket.IO**, showing exactly what you’d write for similar functionality like broadcasting or rooms:\n\n```\n1️⃣ WebSocket (raw)\n\nconst WebSocket = require('ws');\nconst wss = new WebSocket.Server({ port: 4444 });\n\nwss.on('connection', (ws) => {\n  console.log('Client connected');\n\n  // Sending message to this client\n  ws.send('Welcome!');\n\n  // Manual broadcast to all other clients\n  ws.on('message', (message) => {\n    wss.clients.forEach(client => {\n      if (client !== ws && client.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {\n        client.send(`Broadcast: ${message}`);\n      }\n    });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n```\n2️⃣ Socket.IO (with rooms & broadcast)\n\nconst express = require('express');\nconst app = express();\nconst http = require('http').createServer(app);\nconst io = require('socket.io')(http);\n\nio.on('connection', (socket) => {\n  console.log('Client connected');\n\n  // Join a room\n  socket.join('room1');\n\n  // Send to this client\n  socket.emit('message', 'Welcome!');\n\n  // Broadcast to everyone else in room1\n  socket.on('chatMessage', (msg) => {\n    socket.to('room1').emit('message', `Broadcast: ${msg}`);\n  });\n\n  // Broadcast to all except sender (default room)\n  socket.on('globalMessage', (msg) => {\n    socket.broadcast.emit('message', `Global: ${msg}`);\n  });\n});\n\nhttp.listen(4444, () => console.log('Server running on 4444'));\n```\n\n**Key Points in Code Comparison:**\n\n| Feature                   | WebSocket                      | Socket.IO                                 |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Broadcast to all clients  | Manual loop over `wss.clients` | `io.emit()` or `socket.broadcast.emit()`  |\n| Rooms / channels          | Not built-in                   | `socket.join('room')`, `io.to('room')`    |\n| Event-based communication | Only `message` events          | Named events: `socket.on('event')`        |\n| Auto-reconnect            | No                             | Yes, built-in                             |\n| Fallbacks (long polling)  | No                             | Yes, automatically handles older browsers |\n\nThis shows **exactly what extra code you’d have to write in raw WebSocket** vs **Socket.IO where it’s built-in**.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
